@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple BPMN process — start, user task, XOR gateway, end.
'   usecase:      Teach start/intermediate/end events, task, exclusive gateway, sequence flow.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       business-process
' ============================================================================
title Example BPMN Process - Simple Approval

' PlantUML has NO native BPMN. Shape mapping used throughout:
'   circle  (thin)   = start event
'   circle  (double) = intermediate event
'   circle  (thick)  = end event
'   rectangle        = task / activity
'   usecase (diamond)= gateway (XOR/AND/OR/event-based)
'   -->              = sequence flow (solid, same pool)
'   ..>  (dashed)    = message flow (crosses pool boundary)

' --- Events ---------------------------------------------------------------
usecase " " as Start  ' thin circle ~ start event
usecase " " as End    ' thick circle ~ end event (render as end below)
usecase "Approved?" as Xor1
rectangle "Review Request" as Task1

Start --> Task1 : sequence flow
Task1 --> Xor1
Xor1 --> End : (yes)
Xor1 --> Task1 : (no — return to review)

note top of Start
  <b>Start event</b> (thin circle):
  process begins here.
end note

note right of Xor1
  <b>Exclusive gateway (XOR)</b>
  Diamond with X.
  Exactly one outgoing path taken.
end note

note bottom of End
  <b>End event</b> (thick circle):
  process terminates.
end note

note bottom of Task1
  <b>User task</b> (rectangle):
  a human performs this step.
end note

@enduml
